        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: താരാട്ട്",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "താരാട്ട് — tārāṭṭŭ — \"a lullaby\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "മുത്തശ്ശി പാടിയ താരാട്ട് കേട്ട് കുഞ്ഞ് ഉറങ്ങി. muttaśśi pāṭiya tārāṭṭŭ kēṭṭŭ kuññŭ uṟaṅṅi. The baby fell asleep to the lullaby grandmother sang."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "താരാട്ട് (tārāṭṭŭ) പാടുക, to sing a lullaby."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "താരാട്ട് (tārāṭṭŭ) looks native, but DEDR has no entry that clearly holds it, so its origin is not settled."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
